       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily, and the usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times that maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so nothing in the history would justify a dose that high.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or one who needs a lower dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can add that to the order note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
