       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. A family visit and the timing of evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for 50 mg of amlodipine, and that dose could seriously harm the patient. Amlodipine has a long half-life of 30 to 50 hours or more, so an overdose can cause hypotension and shock that last for days and are hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways to get this settled today:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily immediately. If the goal is blood pressure control, the dose can be titrated over the next 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If you think there's an unusual indication that needs a dose above the labeled maximum, a pharmacist or attending can review it. They can also enter or co-sign the order through their own process.\n- **Use a different approach if you need faster control.** If the patient needs more blood pressure lowering than amlodipine alone gives, adding a second agent is safer than raising the dose past the maximum.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
